    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Spectre Jet Pack" hidden="false" id="5e11-3be6-6b8f-75a6">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Spectre Jet Pack" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="cce7-35ab-ad5a-1b64" publicationId="a179-8e8f-4601-987c" page="164">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">A unit composed entirely of models equipped with Spectre Jet Packs may choose to increase its Move Characteristic by +7 and ignore terrain while Moving during the Movement phase. A unit that ends or begins its movement in Dangerous Terrain will still need to take Dangerous Terrain tests as normal, even when employing Spectre Jet Packs, and treats Difficult Terrain as Dangerous Terrain.


In addition to the bonus move during the Movement phase, a unit composed entirely of models with Spectre Jet Packs may make an additional Move of 7” during the Shooting phase. This Move must be taken after the unit has completed any Shooting Attacks, is not limited by the weapons fired by the unit during that Shooting phase and ignores terrain in the same manner as moves made using a Spectre Jet Pack in the Movement phase. During any Reaction that allows a unit to Move, a unit composed entirely of models with Spectre Jump Pack increases the distance of that Move by 7 and allows it to ignore terrain in the same manner as other Spectre Jet Pack moves.


Any model with a Spectre Jet Pack also gains the Bulky (2) and Deep Strike Special Rules. If the model already has the Bulky (2) Special Rule, it gains the Bulky (3) Special Rule instead.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink name="Bulky (X)" id="557b-b42a-f6e7-5cc5" hidden="false" type="rule" targetId="676c-7b75-4b6f-9405">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="Bulky (2)" field="name"/>
          </modifiers>
        </infoLink>
        <infoLink name="Deep Strike" id="3526-35da-7d05-6d5a" hidden="false" type="rule" targetId="f1e1-986f-c783-ca9e"/>
      </infoLinks>
    </selectionEntry>
